  "description": "This gin cocktail from Matthew Biancaniello, formerly of the Library Bar in Los Angeles, is vividly peachy.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: 3 shiso leaves, plus 1 more leaf for garnish (see note)\n\nNotes: The original recipe calls for shiso leaves; if you can't track them down, you can substitute mint, though the flavor won't be quite the same.\nTo make agave syrup, combine 1/4 cup agave nectar with 1/4 cup boiling water. Stir to dissolve. Cool before using. Agave syrup will keep in a sealed container in the refrigerator for up to 5 days.",
